Polaris Enterprise Edition licence
==================================

The contents of the `ee/` directory are NOT covered by the AGPL-3.0-only licence that
governs the rest of this repository (see ../LICENSE). They are made available under the
following terms.

1. Source availability

   The source is published so that it can be read, audited and modified by licensees. It
   is not free or open-source software, and the OSI definition does not apply to it.

2. Grant

   Subject to a current commercial subscription from Peixoto Labs, you may use, modify and
   run this code in production, for your own organisation, on any number of machines
   covered by that subscription.

   Without a current subscription you may read this code, and you may run it for
   development, evaluation and testing. You may not run it in production.

3. Restrictions

   You may not remove or circumvent the licence checks. You may not offer this code, or a
   derivative of it, to third parties as a hosted or managed service.

4. Contributions

   Contributions to `ee/` require the Contributor Licence Agreement in CONTRIBUTING.md,
   which assigns the rights needed to relicense them commercially. This is the mechanism
   that makes dual licensing possible; contributions to the AGPL core do not need it.

5. No warranty

   Provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by law,
   Peixoto Labs is not liable for any claim, damage or other liability arising from its
   use.

Everything outside `ee/` is AGPL-3.0-only. If a file's placement is ambiguous, the
directory it lives in decides — and a file that would be ambiguous belongs in the core.
